  "why": "Calls whose recorded response_sha is not what the cache holds for that request. All of these predate 95d6524, the commit that made a losing write racer adopt the canonical response instead of returning its own. They are unrepairable rather than unfixed: the recorded sha is what the run actually received, so rewriting it would falsify provenance; and a re-roll cannot overwrite the run because code_version is in SEMANTIC_FIELDS, so it lands in a new directory and would put two admissible runs in each affected P3 grid cell. Recorded here so `pi cache verify` fails on a NEW divergence -- which would mean the fix regressed -- rather than on closed history. This list must only ever shrink.",
